    "turn_text": "some really good ideas that would actually do that, bring down the cost. But eliminating all private insurance and eliminating were, you know, coverage by your employer would be an awful idea. I will tell you this, sir. Last week I had breakfast with Alex Acosta. Alex is the, of course, the secretary of labor. And it's the secretary of labor that's overseeing this implementation of the president's executive order on creating association health plans. So if you have an association of farmers, whether it's farmers union or farm bureau, I pick those two groups because they're already in the insurance business They can provide to their association the type of options and the type of plans that large employers can offer and do offer, which is often a very good insurance. That could be true of any association that you're part of or you want to create or join. And so he's going to be coming out with the rules for the association plans here before very long. And he's also accepted my invitation to come in North Dakota and talk about it. So, to me, that's a real grand opportunity, particularly for those entrepreneurs, small business self-employed people, for whom insurance options went down and price went through the roof, particularly the out-of-pocket costs beyond just the premium. The premium was through the roof like Sarah's, but sort of it's copay and high deductible. and things like that. So there's a lot in the works. We've got a lot of work to get it done.",
